WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.357 --> 00:00:19.780
The old brown bear, Baloo, began teaching Mowgli the law of the jungle.

2
00:00:19.781 --> 00:00:24.475
He showed the boy where to find good nuts.

3
00:00:24.476 --> 00:00:31.176
He taught him not to bother Mang, the bat, while he slept during the day.

4
00:00:31.177 --> 00:00:39.613
Mowgli also learned to warn the water snakes before he splashed into their pool.

5
00:00:39.614 --> 00:00:44.868
Each day Bagheera came to check on Mowgli's progress.

6
00:00:44.869 --> 00:00:49.276
"Mowgli is amazing!" Baloo said, beaming.

7
00:00:49.277 --> 00:00:51.952
"He climbs as well as he swims.

8
00:00:51.953 --> 00:00:57.160
And he swims almost as well as he runs."

9
00:00:57.161 --> 00:01:04.156
Baloo made Mowgli work very hard.

10
00:01:04.157 --> 00:01:09.000
One day Mowgli got bored.

11
00:01:09.001 --> 00:01:18.661
When Baloo scolded him for being lazy, Mowgli ran off.

12
00:01:18.662 --> 00:01:22.956
"Where's the boy?" Bagheera asked when he arrived.

13
00:01:22.957 --> 00:01:27.893
Baloo sighed. "He went off in a huff."

14
00:01:27.894 --> 00:01:32.533
"The man cub is very young," Bagheera said.

15
00:01:32.534 --> 00:01:37.501
"Maybe his head is too little to remember all these things."

16
00:01:37.502 --> 00:01:42.239
"Well, he's not too little to be killed!" Baloo replied.

17
00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:45.946
"That's why I'm teaching him the law of the jungle.

18
00:01:45.947 --> 00:01:49.720
He's even learning all of the languages of the jungle.

19
00:01:49.721 --> 00:01:53.235
This will protect him and keep him safe here."

20
00:01:53.236 --> 00:02:00.272
"Maybe." Bagheera stretched out a paw to admire his sharp claws.

21
00:02:00.273 --> 00:02:07.354
"When we find Mowgli, I'll ask him to show you his skill with the languages," Baloo said.

22
00:02:07.355 --> 00:02:10.712
"But who knows when he'll return."

23
00:02:10.713 --> 00:02:15.459
"I'm right here!" a voice snapped from above.

24
00:02:15.460 --> 00:02:20.374
Mowgli slid down a tree trunk and glared at Baloo.

25
00:02:20.375 --> 00:02:23.284
"I only came down because of Bagheera.

26
00:02:23.285 --> 00:02:27.736
I'm still mad at you, fat old Baloo!"

27
00:02:27.737 --> 00:02:33.502
"Show Bagheera how you can speak the jungle languages," Baloo said.

28
00:02:33.503 --> 00:02:38.750
"Which one? I know all of them," Mowgli boasted.

29
00:02:38.751 --> 00:02:43.492
"Okay, great scholar," Baloo teased him.

30
00:02:43.493 --> 00:02:47.092
"Why don't you speak like the lion?"

31
00:02:47.093 --> 00:02:53.475
Mowgli spoke in a deep voice. "We are of one blood."

32
00:02:53.476 --> 00:02:59.206
"Good," Baloo said. "Now speak like a bird."

33
00:02:59.207 --> 00:03:03.169
Mowgli made a hawk's call.

34
00:03:03.170 --> 00:03:07.264
Bagheera was impressed.

35
00:03:07.265 --> 00:03:10.621
"Now the snake's language."

36
00:03:10.622 --> 00:03:15.236
"Ssss!" Mowgli said.

37
00:03:15.237 --> 00:03:20.691
He clapped for his own performance and then jumped onto Bagheera's back.

38
00:03:20.692 --> 00:03:27.145
He banged his heels on the panther's sides while making nasty faces at Baloo.

39
00:03:27.146 --> 00:03:31.507
"Someday you will thank me," Baloo muttered.

40
00:03:31.508 --> 00:03:37.003
"Baloo, how did you learn all the languages?" Bagheera asked.

41
00:03:37.004 --> 00:03:40.985
The bear patted his big furry stomach proudly.

42
00:03:40.986 --> 00:03:44.552
"I learned them from Hathi the elephant."

43
00:03:44.553 --> 00:03:49.993
Meanwhile Mowgli was kicking Bagheera and grabbing at his fur.

44
00:03:49.994 --> 00:03:56.265
"Hey!" Bagheera said. "Watch out for my ribs."

45
00:03:56.266 --> 00:04:01.666
"Someday I'll have a whole tribe of my own," Mowgli bragged.

46
00:04:01.667 --> 00:04:04.358
"I'll lead everyone through the jungle.

47
00:04:04.359 --> 00:04:09.985
I'll play and eat all day long." He laughed.

48
00:04:09.986 --> 00:04:16.754
"And I'll throw branches and dirt at old Baloo."

49
00:04:16.755 --> 00:04:24.754
Whoof! Baloo's big paw scooped Mowgli off Bagheera's back.

50
00:04:24.755 --> 00:04:27.898
"Mowgli!" Baloo said.

51
00:04:27.899 --> 00:04:32.701
"You sound just like the monkeys. You've been spending time with them!"

52
00:04:32.702 --> 00:04:35.130
Mowgli lay on the ground.

53
00:04:35.131 --> 00:04:39.509
He looked at Bagheera, whose eyes had turned cold.

54
00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:41.896
"The monkeys have no laws.

55
00:04:41.897 --> 00:04:46.828
They are rude and silly," Baloo said.

56
00:04:46.829 --> 00:04:49.640
"Stay away from them!"

57
00:04:49.641 --> 00:04:51.672
Mowgli sniffled.

58
00:04:51.673 --> 00:04:54.050
"You were mean to me before.

59
00:04:54.051 --> 00:04:56.213
But the monkeys were nice.

60
00:04:56.214 --> 00:04:59.213
They came down from the trees and played with me.

61
00:04:59.214 --> 00:05:01.995
They gave me nuts too."

62
00:05:01.996 --> 00:05:05.078
Baloo snorted.

63
00:05:05.078 --> 00:05:11.905
"They said I'm going to be their leader one day," Mowgli added spitefully.

64
00:05:11.906 --> 00:05:19.364
"They have no leader," Bagheera snapped. "And they lie."

65
00:05:19.365 --> 00:05:24.143
"Listen, Mowgli." Baloo's voice rumbled like thunder.

66
00:05:24.144 --> 00:05:29.805
"The monkeys live in the trees. They boast and chatter constantly.

67
00:05:29.806 --> 00:05:32.671
We do not drink where the monkeys drink.

68
00:05:32.672 --> 00:05:36.316
We do not go where the monkeys go."

69
00:05:36.317 --> 00:05:38.777
Mowgli lay very still.

70
00:05:38.778 --> 00:05:43.131
"We do not notice them," Baloo added.

71
00:05:43.132 --> 00:05:46.657
"Even when they throw nuts on our heads!"

72
00:05:46.658 --> 00:05:50.936
Just then nuts poured down from the trees.

73
00:05:50.937 --> 00:05:59.876
A bunch of monkeys howled loudly with laughter.
